  "body": "## What\n- replace one executor task per async runtime event with a hard-bounded per-bot event buffer\n- coalesce consecutive `QUEUED` updates to the newest schedule timestamp\n- preserve event ordering through one serialized telemetry drain\n- keep `SESSION_BLOCKED` synchronous and authoritative, with a short-lived per-bot barrier that prevents stale async events from overwriting COOLDOWN\n- add buffer regression tests for coalescing, hard capacity and terminal -> queued ordering\n\n## Why\n`RuntimeTelemetryReporter` used an unbounded single-thread executor queue. If backend telemetry stalled, status events could accumulate without a memory bound. Backend HTTP requests are now time-bounded by #200; this PR also bounds the number of retained telemetry objects themselves without changing marketplace execution semantics.",
  "created_at": "2026-09-14T17:36:12Z",
